  "term": "cholinesterase",
  "definition": "Cholinesterase is a term for enzymes such as acetylcholinesterase and butyrylcholinesterase. In Alzheimer’s disease research, these enzymes are treated as important therapeutic targets, and their activity is often measured to see whether a substance inhibits them.",
